        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-23T22:45:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the barrier is still needed. Once we\u0027ve set mp_state to RUNNABLE, the host may successfully start running this vCPU on another pCPU at any time, i.e. the mp_state check in pkvm_vcpu_run() will succeed even if that check happens on another CPU _right_ after we set mp_state here (i.e. even if the host has issued the vcpu_run hypercall even slightly before that). And that is fine, as long as we still make sure to set up the vCPU in pkvm_vcpu_ap_entry_init() with the correct sipi_vector value, i.e. with the new sipi_vector value we\u0027ve set above. So we need a barrier to make sure pkvm_vcpu_ap_entry_init() sees this new sipi_vector value, not the old (i.e. zero) one, right?",
      "parentUuid": "f763c3b7_8c578e2b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1876,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1877,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "58edd2c95993629f13c1e681f20d4db6b5701387",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
